---
import CalculatorGuideArticle from '../../components/CalculatorGuideArticle.astro';
---

<CalculatorGuideArticle
  toolSlug="probability-calculator"
  label="Probability calculator guide"
  title="How to use the Probability Calculator"
  description="Learn how to use the free Access Free Tools probability calculator for union, intersection, complements, independent events, and steps."
  path="/blog/how-to-use-probability-calculator/"
  intro="The Probability Calculator finds P(A and B), P(A or B), complements, and independent-event intersections from percentage inputs."
  quickStart={[
    'Enter P(A) and P(B) as percentages.',
    'Leave P(A and B) blank for independent events, or enter it when known.',
    'Press Calculate probability.',
    'Review the union, intersection, complements, and formula steps.',
  ]}
  sections={[
    {
      title: 'Independent events',
      paragraphs: [
        'When events are independent, one event does not change the chance of the other. The calculator uses P(A) times P(B) to estimate the intersection.',
        'If you already know the overlap, type it into the intersection field instead of leaving it blank.',
      ],
    },
    {
      title: 'Union and complement',
      paragraphs: [
        'P(A or B) includes event A, event B, or both. The calculator uses P(A) + P(B) - P(A and B).',
        'The complement of A is the chance that A does not happen, which is 100% - P(A).',
      ],
    },
  ]}
  sidecarText="Use the Probability Calculator while you follow the guide."
/>
